{% doc %}
  Tvc Filter Chip

  One category chip above the TVC reel. Selected state is expressed entirely through aria-pressed and
  Tailwind's aria-pressed: variant, so the filter script only ever flips an attribute — never a class.

  Chip Filter and Tvc Category are selects over the same option list, so the two can never drift apart.
  The "all" option is emitted as an empty attribute, which is what the filter logic reads as "no filter"
  without special-casing the value.

  The selected underline is an inset box-shadow, not a border, following the pattern base.css already
  uses on .product-form__submit. A CSS border sits outside the box where Figma's stroke overlaps it, so
  a bordered chip stands 39 against the design's 37 and pushes the whole gallery section 2px over.

  @param {object} block - Tvc Filter Chip block (required)
  @param {boolean} [chip_active] - Render the chip in its selected state (default: false)
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign block = block | default: blank

  unless block != blank
    break
  endunless

  assign chip_label = block.settings.chip_label
  assign chip_filter = block.settings.chip_filter

  if chip_filter == 'all'
    assign chip_filter = ''
  endif
-%}

{%- if chip_label != blank -%}
  <button
    type="button"
    class="tvc-filter-chip shrink-0 rounded-md px-2.5 py-[5px] font-primary text-[14px]/[20px] font-medium text-primary aria-pressed:bg-primary/10 aria-pressed:shadow-[inset_0_-1px_0_0_rgb(var(--color-primary))] lg:px-3.5 lg:text-[18px]/[27px]"
    data-tvc-filter="{{ chip_filter }}"
    aria-pressed="{% if chip_active %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {{- chip_label | escape -}}
  </button>
{%- endif -%}
